{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that the parameter priors for `rho`, `alpha`, and `sigma` appear before those parameters are used to construct the Gaussian-process covariance. Local declarations were split from parameter-dependent assignments to preserve Stan validity and the same posterior density. No data changes were made.
","model_safe_stan":"// Fit the hyperparameters of a Gaussian process with an 
// exponentiated quadratic kernel

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] mu = rep_vector(0, N);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  matrix[N, N] L_K;
  matrix[N, N] K;
  real sq_sigma;

  rho ~ inv_gamma(5, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  K = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho);
  sq_sigma = square(sigma);

  // diagonal elements
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    K[n, n] = K[n, n] + sq_sigma;
  }

  L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);

  y ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mu, L_K);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":2,"x":[5.154505073719477,2.9864731177847794],"y":[2.0,2.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
